-- ============================================================================================================
-- tests-independent.l4: INDEPENDENT TEST AUTHOR's assertions for the Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 encoding.
-- Expected values are decided from the source text in ANSWERS.md (written BEFORE any .l4 file was opened).
-- Scenario numbers refer to ANSWERS.md. A letter suffix (12a, 12b) splits one scenario into several asks.
-- Convention: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING for MAYBE BOOLEAN; JUST n / NOTHING for MAYBE NUMBER.
-- An expected value was changed after a first run only where the comment says AUTHOR CORRECTION; each such change is also listed in the Errata
-- at the end of ANSWERS.md with the reason taken from the source text. Every other failing assertion is left failing on purpose.
-- Layer 1 asserts the encoding's own functions; the seat layer (S1.nn to S4.nn, from the first, second, third and fourth quarter of the text)
-- asserts the person-facing functions in snap-seat. Scenarios with no function are shown as comment lines saying GAP.
-- ============================================================================================================
