#ASSERT `s 2015(d)(1)(A) the individual is ineligible to participate in the program` 30 TRUE (`s 2015(d)(1)(A) conduct` WITH `refuses to register for employment at the time of application and every 12 months thereafter` IS FALSE, `refuses to participate in an employment and training program to the extent required by the State agency` IS FALSE, `refuses to accept an offer of employment` IS FALSE, `the offer is at a site or plant not subject to a strike or lockout at the time of the refusal` IS FALSE, `the hourly wage offered, in dollars` IS 0, `the applicable Federal or State minimum hourly wage, in dollars` IS 0, `the hourly wage that would have governed had the Fair Labor Standards Act minimum rate applied, in dollars` IS 0, `refuses to provide the State agency with sufficient information to determine employment status or job availability` IS FALSE, `voluntarily quits a job` IS FALSE, `voluntarily reduces work effort` IS TRUE, `hours worked per week after the reduction` IS 29, `fails to comply with section 2029` IS FALSE, `there was good cause` IS (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 199b s 2015(d)(1)(A)(v)(II): voluntarily and without good cause reduces work to 29 hours a week; AUTHOR CORRECTION after the first run (see Errata): my record left the MAYBE field "there was good cause" at NOTHING, but the scenario says "without good cause"
#ASSERT `s 2015(d)(1)(B) the longest period of household ineligibility the State agency may determine, in days` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE 365 EQUALS JUST 180 -- 200a s 2015(d)(1)(B): the head of the household became ineligible for 365 days; the household's period is no more than the lesser of that and 180 days
#ASSERT `s 2015(d)(1)(B) the longest period of household ineligibility the State agency may determine, in days` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE 90 EQUALS JUST 90 -- 200b s 2015(d)(1)(B): the head's period is 90 days
